{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493119-combining-horrid-form-the-skin-of-the-adder-black-metamorphosis-etc","id":1493119,"title":"Combining Horrid Form, The Skin of the Adder, Black Metamorphosis etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-15T09:59:20-07:00","id":1493119,"title":"Combining Horrid Form, The Skin of the Adder, Black Metamorphosis etc.","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I was wondering how people run these transformations in the very rare case a vampire uses multiple of them.<br /> Personally I think Shape of the Beast Wraths and Horrid Form are not compatible, but everything else is. <br /> For example I could see Horrid Form, Skin of the Adder and Black metamorphosis being compatible.<br /> Likewise for Shape of the Beast Wraths, Skin of the Adder and Black metamorphosis. <br /> <br /> What do you think? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2024-malfi","name":"Malfi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T19:01:00-07:00","id":1493139,"title":"","content":"Easy: If they could logically go together (say, Skin of the Adder and Protean Claws) they get them both. If they do not logically go together, (Tenebrous Form and Skin of the Adder) the one activated first takes precedence. <br /> <br /> If they go together, all mechanical advantages and disadvantages stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T21:56:57-07:00","id":1493150,"title":"","content":"Not sure which edition we are talking.<br /> If it is pre V5 editions, I think Protean 4 is the only power they explicitly say that you can't use it together with Shape of the Beast with Serpentis and Vicissitude powers.<br /> <br /> Appart from the I would say the full body transformations that turn ito some kind of monster or animal, like Horrid Form, Shape of the Beast Wraths, The Form of the Cobra and Typhonic Avatar don't stack with each other, but with partial transformation like The Tongue of the Asp, Skin of the Adder, Feral Claws if the form has the necessary limps (so no feral claws with Form of the Cobra).<br /> <br /> And powers like Bloodform, Mist Form and Tenebrous Form that turn you incorporal just suppress the other powers, but if you activate them while transformed, you could still be transformed if you end them, if the duration of the other power is long enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T22:27:46-07:00","id":1493152,"title":"","content":"Honestly, rules be damned, I think wolf form and horrid form should be compatible. Horrid wolf form would be nothing short of Gnarly. But yeah rules wise you're explicitly not supposed to do it. <br /> <br /> <br /> Skin of the adder would be compatible with all. As would BM if rules don't say otherwise. I might rule that BM and other Obtenebration uses your unmodified strength should it be combined with Horrid form. Things like Tenebrous form or bloodform would probably cause all modifications to be irrelevant while active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T08:56:42-07:00","id":1493162,"title":"","content":"A Vampire with multiple unique disciplines that involve body alteration? If I'm putting an NPC like this I assure you that by design is to make the player crew face a real monster. A diablerist, a diabolist, a failed Tremere experiment, a methuselah or something like that. So why put all these powers together if not for showing them? So I would make them all stack, because they are there for a reason.<br /> <br /> But if the reason is only that this NPC has multiple backup plans, there is no need to show them all together. Or for this NPC these powers don't stack. And so the stack problem is not a real problem.<br /> <br /> This is such a fringe and power cranked situation that you can have a case-by-case approach.<br /> <br /> tl:dr - check the reason for that NPC existence than decide if the powers stack or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26404-submariner93","name":"Submariner93","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26404_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T10:28:45-07:00","id":1493170,"title":"","content":"Is there anything saying an abomination can't use crinos form and horror form together? I assume you can't but really just not sure.<br /> <br /> Sure I'd let an npc op villians do this but that's up to a gm","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19506-killtron","name":"Killtron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T11:37:04-07:00","id":1493175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Submariner93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493119-combining-horrid-form-the-skin-of-the-adder-black-metamorphosis-etc?p=1493162#post1493162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Vampire with multiple unique disciplines that involve body alteration? </div> </div> </div> </div>I think 2 at high level (4+) isn't a massive stretch. Plus IMO Protean, Serpentis, Visceraticka and thanatosis are very related disciplines and very mutable disciplines and i wouldn't think it a stretch if a master of one started developing powers equivalent to one of the other Protean-like disciplines. <br /> <br /> You'd get more mileage out of common disciplines, certainly. But a metamorphosist or someone else strange enough might develop both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-17T17:25:30-07:00","id":1493224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killtron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493119-combining-horrid-form-the-skin-of-the-adder-black-metamorphosis-etc?p=1493170#post1493170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anything saying an abomination can't use crinos form and horror form together? I assume you can't but really just not sure.<br /> <br /> Sure I'd let an npc op villians do this but that's up to a gm</div> </div> </div> </div>Abominations are not made to answer classic rules, they're combining 2 differents system and will work differently depending on which you use. The Black Hand book give some indication while the Changings Breeds book give other<br /> <br /> Can they use Disciplines transformation in addition to their native? Only the ST can decide, i would certainly to create a bat winged crinos of 4 meter with absurd power, a perfect main antagonist fo a campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T10:30:40-07:00","id":1493249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Submariner93</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1493119-combining-horrid-form-the-skin-of-the-adder-black-metamorphosis-etc?p=1493162#post1493162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Vampire with multiple unique disciplines that involve body alteration?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are combination disciplines for these disciplines in the rules, and in older Editions the were even 2 revenant families that had Protean and Vicissitude, so it is not completly insane.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}